course: dictionary
lesson: 1848
title: Cockpit: where the pilot sits
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A cockpit is the place at the front of a plane where the pilot sits and flies it. Use the words around it to check. «Children may sometimes visit a plane's cockpit, but only trained pilots fly the plane.» The pilots fly from there, so the cockpit must be where the flying happens.
explain: A cockpit can be a copy too. «Think of a pilot in a flight simulator: the cockpit is a model, but the skill is real.» A simulator is a practice machine, so the cockpit inside it is a model of the real one. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: The same word can mean a small space in other vehicles. A racing car driver sits in a cockpit, and a small boat or spaceship can have one too. Look at the words around the word to see which kind the writer means.
fact: A cockpit is the front part of an aeroplane, where the pilot sits and flies it.
fact: A cockpit can also be the small space where a racing car driver sits.
fact: On a small boat or spaceship, the cockpit is the steering area.
fact: «Cockpit sounds» are recorded inside the black box, which is painted bright orange so it can be found.
fact: Long ago, a cockpit was also a pit or ring where cockfights were held, but this meaning is old and rare today.
exercise: «Children may sometimes visit a plane's cockpit, but only trained pilots fly the plane.» Where do pilots sit to fly a plane? | *In the cockpit | In the back seats with the passengers | In the galley, near the food | In the luggage hold
exercise: What is a cockpit in a racing car? | The wheels and tyres | *The small space where the driver sits | The boot, where bags are kept | The pipe where the smoke comes out
exercise: Isaac's friend's dad is a pilot. Which phrase names a door that is locked for safety on airliners? | cabin door | *cockpit door | shed door | garden gate
test: «The black box is really two tough recorders, one for flight data and one for cockpit sounds.» In this sentence, cockpit sounds means | *Sounds from the front of the plane, where the pilots sit | Sounds from under the sea | Sounds from the food trolley | Music played at the airport
test: A small boat has a cockpit too. What does cockpit mean on a small boat? | *The steering area where the person sits | The sail at the top of the mast | The cabin where the cook sleeps | The anchor at the front
exam: Which meaning fits best in «Think of a pilot in a flight simulator: the cockpit is a model, but the skill is real»? | A bag for carrying tools | A kind of bird that lives on farms | An old pit where cockfights were held | *A copy of the front of a plane where a pilot practises
